> as {na} and C1 being a consonant, and define another rafsi R2 whose first
> consonant is C2. If C1+R2 is morphologically acceptable,
.skamyxatra

Morphologically acceptable *as a {lujvo}* (which usually only applies when =
R2
is a string of more than one {rafsi}).

> then to form lujvo R1+R2 we need a y in between C1 and C2, even if C1+C2 =
is
> an acceptable consonant cluster, to avoid fragmentation into M1 C1+R2?

Yes.  This is known as the "tosmabru test," described in item 5 of the
{lujvo}-making algorithm in section 4.11 of the CLL.  Note that item 5a of =
the
description is incorrect; the first sentence should read, "Examine all the =
C/C
consonant pairs up to the first 'y'-hyphen, or up to the end of the word in
case there are no 'y'-hyphens."

